      "client"
    ],
    "frame": "client"
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "IKE_SA_INIT",
      "desc": "Agree on algorithms, swap keys",
      "detail": "The VPN client opens with IKE on UDP port 500. Its first message proposes the algorithms (AES-GCM with 256-bit keys, SHA-256, Curve25519) and carries a public key and a random nonce; the gateway picks the proposal and sends its own key and nonce. Both now share a secret, but neither has proved who it is yet.",
      "facts": [
        [
          "Port",
          "UDP 500"
        ],
        [
          "Proposed",
          "AES-GCM-256, Curve25519"
        ],
        [
          "After this",
          "Shared keys, no identities"
        ]
      ],
      "events": [
        {
          "type": "show",
          "nodes": [
            "router",
            "internet",
            "relay"
          ],
          "frame": "relay"
        },
        {
          "type": "packet",
          "from": "client",
          "to": "relay",
          "color": "amber",
          "label": "IKE_SA_INIT",
          "payload": [
            "proposal, key, nonce",
            "NAT detection"
          ],
          "row": {
            "time": "0.000s",
            "src": "192.168.1.10",
            "dst": "192.0.2.51",
            "proto": "ISAKMP",
            "info": "IKE_SA_INIT MID=00 Initiator Request",
            "len": "242 B",
            "wire": {
              "udp": {
                "sport": 500,
                "dport": 500,
                "data": {
                  "ike": {
                    "exchange": 34,
                    "spiI": 9167668316052413000
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "packet",
          "from": "relay",
          "to": "client",
          "color": "amber",
          "label": "IKE_SA_INIT",
          "payload": [
            "chosen proposal, key, nonce"
          ],
          "row": {
            "time": "0.017s",
            "src": "192.0.2.51",
            "dst": "192.168.1.10",
            "proto": "ISAKMP",
            "info": "IKE_SA_INIT MID=00 Responder Response",
            "len": "242 B",
            "wire": {
              "udp": {
                "sport": 500,
                "dport": 500,
                "data": {
                  "ike": {
                    "exchange": 34,
                    "response": true,
                    "spiI": 9167668316052413000,
                    "spiR": 3201509163735963600
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "A NAT in the Way",
      "desc": "So everything moves to port 4500",
      "detail": "Both messages also carried hashes of the address and port each side sent from. At the gateway they don’t match what arrived: the home router rewrote the laptop’s address on the way (NAT). ESP has no port numbers, so a NAT can’t pass it; both sides move to UDP port 4500 and wrap ESP in UDP from now on.",
      "facts": [
        [
          "Hashes of",
          "Address and port sent from"
        ],
        [
          "Mismatch",
          "The router rewrote them"
        ],
        [
          "Fix",
          "Everything over UDP 4500"
        ]
      ],
      "events": [
        {
          "type": "note",
          "at": "router",
          "text": "NAT DETECTED",
          "tone": "amber"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "IKE_AUTH",
      "desc": "Prove who you are, encrypted",
      "detail": "Now encrypted, each side sends its identity, its certificate and a signature over everything said so far, so anyone in the middle would be caught. The laptop asks for an address inside the network and gets 10.8.0.2. The same exchange sets up the ESP tunnel itself, with its own keys and an SPI for each direction.",
      "facts": [
        [
          "Port",
          "UDP 4500 (NAT traversal)"
        ],
        [
          "Proves",
          "Identity, by certificate"
        ],
        [
          "Laptop gets",
          "10.8.0.2, and a DNS server"
        ]
      ],
      "events": [
        {
          "type": "packet",
          "from": "client",
          "to": "relay",
          "color": "amber",
          "label": "IKE_AUTH",
          "payload": [
            "identity, certificate",
            "signature"
          ],
          "row": {
            "time": "0.034s",
            "src": "192.168.1.10",
            "dst": "192.0.2.51",
            "proto": "ISAKMP",
            "info": "IKE_AUTH MID=01 Initiator Request",
            "len": "1230 B",
            "wire": {
              "udp": {
                "sport": 4500,
                "dport": 4500,
                "data": {
                  "ike": {
                    "exchange": 35,
                    "nonEsp": true,
                    "spiI": 9167668316052413000,
                    "spiR": 3201509163735963600,
                    "first": 35,
                    "sealed": 1128,
                    "inner": [
                      "IDi, CERT, AUTH: who the laptop is, proven",
                      "CP: asks for an inside address and DNS",
                      "SA: what to use for ESP (AES-GCM)",
                      "TSi, TSr: which traffic goes in the tunnel"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "locked": true
        },
        {
          "type": "packet",
          "from": "relay",
          "to": "client",
          "color": "amber",
          "label": "IKE_AUTH",
          "payload": [
            "identity, certificate",
            "address 10.8.0.2"
          ],
          "row": {
            "time": "0.052s",
            "src": "192.0.2.51",
            "dst": "192.168.1.10",
            "proto": "ISAKMP",
            "info": "IKE_AUTH MID=01 Responder Response",
            "len": "1182 B",
            "wire": {
              "udp": {
                "sport": 4500,
                "dport": 4500,
                "data": {
                  "ike": {
                    "exchange": 35,
                    "nonEsp": true,
                    "response": true,
                    "spiI": 9167668316052413000,
                    "spiR": 3201509163735963600,
                    "first": 36,
                    "sealed": 1080,
                    "inner": [
                      "IDr, CERT, AUTH: who the gateway is, proven",
                      "CP: inside address 10.8.0.2, DNS 10.8.0.1",
                      "SA: ESP with AES-GCM, and the SPIs",
                      "TSi, TSr: everything (0.0.0.0/0)"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "locked": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Into the Tunnel",
      "desc": "The whole packet, encrypted",
      "detail": "You open https://www.example.com, looked up through the tunnel at the DNS server the gateway gave (not shown). The SYN from 10.8.0.2 is encrypted whole into an ESP packet: an SPI that names the tunnel, a sequence number, then the encrypted packet and a check value, all inside UDP port 4500. Its UDP checksum is zero: ESP checks its own contents.",
      "facts": [
        [
          "SPI",
          "Names the tunnel"
        ],
        [
          "Inside",
          "The whole IP packet"
        ],
        [
          "Overhead",
          "62 bytes + padding"
        ]
      ],
      "events": [
        {
          "type": "packet",
          "from": "client",
