            "src": "192.168.1.10",
            "dst": "192.0.2.51",
            "proto": "ESP",
            "info": "ESP (SPI=0xc5a1e7d2)",
            "len": "130 B",
            "wire": {
              "udp": {
                "sport": 4500,
                "dport": 4500,
                "data": {
                  "esp": {
                    "spi": 3315722194,
                    "seq": 1,
                    "sealed": 56,
                    "inner": [
                      "IPv4 10.8.0.2 → 203.0.113.10",
                      "TCP 52344 → 443 [SYN]",
                      "then padding, pad length and next header (4)"
                    ]
                  }
                },
                "noChecksum": true
              }
            }
          },
          "locked": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Out and Back",
      "desc": "Through the gateway and home again",
      "detail": "The gateway decrypts the packet and sends the SYN on from its own address, one hop older. The answer comes back to the gateway and returns through the tunnel as another ESP packet, with the SPI for the laptop’s direction and its own sequence numbers.",
